    "body": "Depends on: #64. The legacy runtime penalizes recently-emitted tokens via the recency Vec (now TokenState); the graph scorer has no equivalent, so greedy graph generation can loop. Add a bounded, integer-only repetition mechanism to the graph scorer (recency window penalty in ScoreQ, or coverage-aware suppression), measured by repetition rate on a fixed probe set. Acceptance: repetition rate reported in score_report.json; no quality regression on Gate C; allocation-free and integer-only.\n\n\n---\n\n## Definition of Done\n- A bounded, integer-only repetition mechanism exists in the graph scorer (ScoreQ recency penalty or coverage-aware suppression).\n- Repetition rate is measured and reported without Gate C quality regression.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] Repetition rate on a fixed probe set is reported in score_report.json (before vs after).\n- [ ] Gate C top-1 agreement and bits/token unchanged within noise.\n- [ ] The mechanism is allocation-free and integer-only (census + source scan).",
